Subject: [PATCH 34/37] s13d g4 cont4: the rightward rebalance row; four proofs
 the seal test caught
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The rightward row: the scan as a pinned test with its two exits, the found path widened to the
row's box and composed with the count's clear, and the short path, through the pinned branch
(which, with its seam and way-back lemmas, now takes a test that moves its pin). Restated on the
data at its own scratch start, it is a contract with the target's fields at dir = true for every
C ≥ 2300.

The seal test caught four proofs that reduced another file's definitions: the segment-built
re-index (Contract.ofSegment's precondition, now through Contract.ofSegment_pre), the seam's
way back (Contract.seq_pre), a host round (Cfg.mapState_state) and the pass contract
(headBox_iff).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0155fKrzMUhziJHzQxJacYbw
